
Batch-flow contract checks

Run from the repository root:
	python Codigo/test/test_batch_contract.py

The script uses the real PendingBatch and CircularBuffer definitions and the
initRtcBuffer, processBatch and finalizeBatch bodies from main.cpp. Radio and
SD operations are simulated. The buffer and flow are made constexpr only in
the test copy so a GNU C++ compiler can evaluate the scenarios at compile time.
No test binary or temporary source file is written.

The compiler is selected through --compiler, CXX, g++ in PATH, or the usual
Windows PlatformIO Xtensa compiler location. Python standard library only.

These checks do not validate actual radio transmission, physical RTC retention,
SD write integrity, GNSS, power consumption or the soil sensor. A source-level
guard checks that SD::logBatch rejects short writes before counting a line; it
does not simulate filesystem errors, partial card writes or power loss.
